From 623d51d1bb2dce501a379b28a6a341d7f7955eee Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 21:15:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(gridforge): intake pipeline, CLI, model pack, Density
 Screen and Portfolio Screen

Patch 0003. Turns the engine into a delivery machine: one JSON file per hall in,
a priced engagement out. This is the leverage step - everything that used to be
retyped per project now happens once, so project N+1 costs a fraction of project 1.

    python3 -m gridforge init   -o intake.json      blank pack to send a client
    python3 -m gridforge gaps      intake.json      the data request
    python3 -m gridforge screen    intake.json -o out   EUR 4,500 Density Screen
    python3 -m gridforge study     intake.json -o out   EUR 22-45k Envelope Study
    python3 -m gridforge portfolio halls/*.json -o out  EUR 60-140k Portfolio Screen

INTAKE AND THE DATA-GAP LEDGER (gridforge/intake/)

- A declarative intake document: 16 declared fields, 13 of them required before a
  study can be issued. A value may be a bare number or {value, evidence, note,
  source} where the customer wants to qualify it.
- Anything not supplied falls back to a library default AND is recorded as a gap
  carrying why it binds and where the customer can get it. The gap list is a
  deliverable in its own right: "here are the eleven numbers that decide your
  answer, seven of which nobody has measured" is what sells the study from the
  screen.
- A fallback can never masquerade as customer data - supplied values are E5,
  fallbacks are E0, and a test enforces it. An empty transformer or UPS schedule
  counts as missing, not as supplied.
- IntakeReport.can_issue gates ISSUED mode; engagement_recommendation says which
  product to sell against this intake.

DELIVERY (gridforge/cli.py, gridforge/serialize.py)

- Scenarios are now data in the intake, not code in an example: the standard five
  (retained air, RDHx, hybrid DLC, full DLC, full DLC + behind-the-meter), each
  selectable per project.
- Seven generic sensitivity knobs applicable to any site, run against the relieved
  case.
- model_pack.json: inputs, gaps, scenarios, ladder, energisation curve, economics
  and the provenance digest of every headline number. It ships to the client - it
  is what lets them re-run our conclusion when their inputs change.
- Bad intake exits 2 with a one-line error, not a traceback. A failed report gate
  exits 3 and writes nothing.

TWO NEW SELLABLE ARTEFACTS

- Density Screen (reporting/screen.py): the five-day door-opener. Binding
  constraint, first six rungs, time to power, and the data request. Short on
  purpose, and worth its fee on its own.
- Portfolio Screen (reporting/portfolio.py): N halls ranked by one methodology,
  with a portfolio-level view of which constraint binds across several halls -
  because a shared constraint is a programme, not a site problem. Highest revenue
  per founder-hour in the ladder, since only the inputs change.

On the four synthetic reference halls: 225 deployable racks across the portfolio,
Oslo first at 88 racks, London last at 6 racks but energised in 36 weeks rather
than 160. The three ranking objectives disagree, which is the point - a test fails
if they ever agree, because an objective that changes nothing is decoration.

62 tests pass, up from 43. Still no third-party dependency at import time.

